NEARS-2137 QA — regression-candidate confirmation (NOT this ticket's scope)
fetchStoreTax (checkout_controller.dart ~:1145-1165) double-emits [FAIL]
independently of the getOrderTax fix in this ticket. Confirmed live via a
throwaway test using the identical real-client harness pattern
(_FixedStatusClient + _SpyRecorder implements CrashRecorder), built, run,
and deleted (not committed) during this QA pass.

RESULT:
302 -> 2 recordError entries:
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/order/get-Tax http_status=302 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response"
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/order/get-Tax http_status=302 type=ApiFailure msg="checkout: group per-store tax non-200"
500 -> 2 recordError entries:
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/order/get-Tax http_status=500 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response"
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/order/get-Tax http_status=500 type=ApiFailure msg="checkout: group per-store tax non-200"

MECHANISM (matches comment 15160 Finding 2): fetchStoreTax calls
checkoutServiceInterface.getOrderTax(taxBody, handleError: false) but the
checkout_service/checkout_repository getOrderTax signature never exposes/
threads a `logError` param to ApiClient.postData, so postData's own
`logError` default (true) still fires api_client.dart's generic
"unhandled api response" AppLogger.failure INSIDE handleResponse — a
SEPARATE emitter from fetchStoreTax's own explicit
AppLogger.failure('checkout: group per-store tax non-200', ...) call
immediately after. Two independent emitters, one event — same double-emit
FAMILY as this ticket but a DIFFERENT call site/mechanism (getOrderTax's
own is a single emitter, checkApi, invoked twice).

Confirmed as a genuine, live, reproducible regression candidate. Explicitly
OUT of NEARS-2137's scope per the description and comment 15370. Routed via
the standard QA-confirms -> PO-files-linked-Bug chain (regression_bugs[]),
not fixed here.
